WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.492
Sustained wind is a more continuous flow, while gusts are shorter increases or shifts.

00:00:05.492 --> 00:00:11.269
Gust spread matters because an aircraft may appear stable between gusts yet briefly lose position,

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:13.580
altitude, image stability, or control margin.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.046
Plan outbound and return legs with direction in mind.

00:00:17.046 --> 00:00:20.127
A tailwind outbound may become a headwind home,

00:00:20.127 --> 00:00:22.438
reducing groundspeed and increasing battery demand.

00:00:22.438 --> 00:00:26.289
Reserve energy for changing direction, route adjustment, approach, and landing.

00:00:26.289 --> 00:00:30.911
Airflow near buildings, trees, ridges, coastlines, cliffs, and terrain can accelerate, roll,

00:00:30.911 --> 00:00:32.451
descend, or become turbulent.

00:00:32.451 --> 00:00:36.302
Open fields can also experience strong gusts and thermal movement.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.613
Conditions vary with altitude and position.

00:00:38.613 --> 00:00:40.154
Watch actual aircraft behavior.

00:00:40.154 --> 00:00:44.390
Increased tilt, poor position hold, low groundspeed, rising power use, vibration,

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:49.397
or unstable footage can reveal conditions more severe than the launch area suggested.

00:00:49.397 --> 00:00:52.478
Do not normalize repeated warnings or control corrections.

00:00:52.478 --> 00:00:56.329
Payload size and shape can increase drag and change response.

00:00:56.329 --> 00:00:59.025
Manufacturer wind figures are not mission targets.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:01.336
Darkness, obstacles, narrow routes, inexperienced crew,

00:01:01.336 --> 00:01:04.417
or limited landing options justify lower operational thresholds.

00:01:04.417 --> 00:01:08.654
Crosswind during approach can also complicate landing near obstacles or people.

00:01:08.654 --> 00:01:13.275
Plan an approach direction with room to stabilize and go around or

00:01:13.275 --> 00:01:15.586
divert before battery pressure becomes urgent.

00:01:15.586 --> 00:01:20.208
Cancel or delay when gusts or turbulence threaten stable control, safe return,

00:01:20.208 --> 00:01:21.363
or usable data.

00:01:21.363 --> 00:01:23.289
If conditions worsen in flight,

00:01:23.289 --> 00:01:27.140
turn back early while battery and landing choices remain generous.
